  "about_expertise_text": "We don't claim credentials we don't have. What we can tell you is how this site works: every test tool is built to do one specific, verifiable thing (cycle through color panels, render a gradient, flash a stuck pixel at high speed), and every guide is checked against manufacturer specifications and established display-industry standards rather than written to sound authoritative. We're also upfront about limits - a browser-based test is genuinely useful for spotting dead pixels, uniformity issues, and color casts, but it can't replace a hardware colorimeter for calibrated color accuracy or a lab rig for millisecond-precise response times, and we say so on the pages where that matters.",
